{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":true,"promptId":"c88cddde-d9ec-4df1-89bf-4cd0fc5db786","agentId":"acb0e47c9637c321b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"Repo C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers (FastAPI cuore/; mes lib only via cuore/services/*_bridge.py). Python .venv\\Scripts\\python.exe. No subagents, no commits, no Edge, minimal grepping. Report under 100 words. You own: mes-log-mcp/mes/systems.py (additive only), mes-log-mcp/mes/jobs.py (additive), mes-log-mcp/mes/mechanic_tests.py, cuore/services/jobs_bridge.py, cuore/services/electrical_bridge.py, cuore/services/tests_bridge.py, and system_states() inside cuore/services/systems_map_bridge.py (another agent adds new functions to that file; touch only system_states and helpers it alone uses; re-read the file before each edit), new test cuore/tests/check_system_vocab.py. Do not edit templates, routes, system_detail_bridge.py, job.js/css.\n\nGoal A, shared vocabulary: the 25 system keys in mes.systems are the single taxonomy. Add mes.systems.normalize_system(text) -> key|None (exact key, label, known aliases such as the electrical layout tags and free-text like \"EVAP\", \"evap system\", \"Evaporative emissions\"; keep an explicit alias table, no fuzzy guessing beyond case/punctuation/alias). Then: hypotheses store a normalized `system` key on add/edit (keep the original text in `system_text`); jobs_bridge filters by key; electrical_bridge exposes elements_for_system(key) using the alias table instead of ad-hoc tag matching (look at how system_detail_bridge.py currently maps systems-key<->electrical tag and move that map into mes.systems as the canonical alias table so both use one source; leave system_detail_bridge.py itself for its owner, but keep its import names working); mechanic_tests.systems values must all be valid keys (validate at load). Migration: old hypotheses with free-text system normalize on read; never rewrite the JSONL log in place.\nGoal B, per-system VERIFIED_CLEAN: in systems_map_bridge.system_states(), a system is VERIFIED_CLEAN only when its own codes are all cleared AND its OBD monitor (if it has one; map monitor names to system keys in mes.systems, e.g. EVAP->evap, CAT->exhaust/catalyst, O2/O2 heater->fuel or exhaust per the table, misfire->ignition, fuel system->fuel) reads complete from a readiness read that came from the car (serial stream; dossier_bridge readiness_panel marks source), with no code back since. Systems with no monitor stay CLEARED_UNVERIFIED until a car scan after the clear shows no code back for that system. Never derive VERIFIED_CLEAN from the whole-car verdict.\nTest: normalize_system covers 25 keys + labels + at least 12 aliases + None for junk; hypothesis add with \"Evap system\" stores system=\"evap\"; every mechanic_tests systems entry is a key; system_states with a fixture readiness (EVAP incomplete, codes cleared) gives CLEARED_UNVERIFIED, and with EVAP complete from the car and no code back gives VERIFIED_CLEAN; a demo-source readiness never gives VERIFIED_CLEAN. Run it plus check_jobs_rules.py, check_tests_page.py, check_systems_map_api.py, check_system_page.py."},"uuid":"2eb8a826-136c-4c9e-a3f5-36085b5c5d72","timestamp":"2026-10-08T23:40:11.452Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
