{"parentUuid":"f727e06b-461f-4875-8ac6-330aee1dc357","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"acb0e47c9637c321b","attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[{"name":"SubagentHandback","description":"Deliver your final report to the agent that spawned you (your caller). Use it once, for that hand-off only: when your work is complete, call SubagentHandback({message: <your full report>}) as your last tool call and then stop. It is not a messaging channel: do not use it for progress updates or questions.\n\nOnly a report delivered through SubagentHandback reaches your caller; plain text you write at the end of your turn is NOT delivered. There is no recipient parameter: the report can only go to your caller.","input_schema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","type":"object","properties":{"message":{"description":"Your full report for your caller","type":"string"}},"required":["message"],"additionalProperties":false},"eager_input_streaming":true,"defer_loading":true}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"953ae758-91a2-4a62-8933-274ccb5b7bf6","timestamp":"2026-10-09T00:19:40.581Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"953ae758-91a2-4a62-8933-274ccb5b7bf6","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"acb0e47c9637c321b","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CfqhqCT8SVXfxQV4ucr2B","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TGAwrznkA31nuzXYNZQ8nn","name":"SubagentHandback","input":{"message":"All 5 required test suites pass in a fresh combined run (exit code 0): check_system_vocab.py 19/19 (new), check_jobs_rules.py 27/27, check_tests_page.py 28/28, check_systems_map_api.py 16/16, check_system_page.py 82/82.\n\nGoal A (shared vocabulary) — mes-log-mcp/mes/systems.py: added normalize_system(text), backed by an ALIASES table (electrical-layout tags + free text/OBD monitor names) and a new ELEMENT_TAGS_FOR table (the canonical move of system_detail_bridge.py's _ELEMENT_TAGS_FOR; that file itself was left untouched per instructions, so it still has its own local copy — its owner can later point it at mes.systems.ELEMENT_TAGS_FOR). mes-log-mcp/mes/jobs.py: hypotheses now store a normalized `system` key plus the original `system_text` on add/edit; old JSONL records with no system_text are migrated on read inside _fold() — the log itself is never rewritten. mes-log-mcp/mes/mechanic_tests.py needed no change: _t() already validates every systems entry against SYSTEMS at import time. cuore/services/jobs_bridge.py: added a _sys_key() helper and used it in _augment_with_liveboard and _next_unresolved_test so hypothesis/suggestion/open-work \"system\"/\"family\" strings compare through the shared taxonomy instead of raw .lower(). cuore/services/electrical_bridge.py: added elements_for_system(key), resolving via mes.systems.normalize_system/ELEMENT_TAGS_FOR instead of ad-hoc tag matching.\n\nGoal B (per-system VERIFIED_CLEAN) — mes-log-mcp/mes/systems.py also gained MONITOR_TO_SYSTEM, system_for_monitor(), monitors_for_system() (OBD-II Mode 01 monitor names -> system keys). cuore/services/systems_map_bridge.py's system_states() (only that function and its own new helpers _workup/_readiness_panel were touched) now requires, per system: own codes cleared (no ACTIVE) AND either no monitor (stays CLEARED_UNVERIFIED) or the relevant monitor(s) complete on a from-car dossier_bridge.readiness_panel reading (VERIFIED_CLEAN); the whole-car verdict is no longer consulted anywhere in this function.\n\nNew test cuore/tests/check_system_vocab.py covers: all 25 keys/labels + 16 aliases + junk/blank -> None; hypothesis add/edit normalization and old-record migration; mechanic_tests systems-vocabulary validity; and the three system_states scenarios (EVAP incomplete -> CLEARED_UNVERIFIED, EVAP complete from the car -> VERIFIED_CLEAN, demo-source readiness never -> VERIFIED_CLEAN), plus a no-monitor-system guard — using a synthetic by_system/dossier fixture (the real Stelvio corpus's EVAP codes are ACTIVE/returned, not CLEARED_UNVERIFIED, so it couldn't serve as the fixture for this specific check) with a deliberately VERIFIED_CLEAN whole-car verdict to prove no shortcut is taken.\n\nOne note for the template owner: job.html renders `h.system` directly (line 211/207) for display; that now shows the normalized lowercase key (e.g. \"evap\", or \"engine_management\" for a \"misfire\" family hypothesis) instead of the raw text a mechanic typed. The original text is preserved in the new `system_text` field for exactly this case — the template can switch to showing that instead when convenient. I did not touch job.html (templates are off-limits per my scope).\n\nFiles touched: mes-log-mcp/mes/systems.py, mes-log-mcp/mes/jobs.py, cuore/services/jobs_bridge.py, cuore/services/electrical_bridge.py, cuore/services/systems_map_bridge.py (system_states + its own helpers only), cuore/tests/check_system_vocab.py (new). mechanic_tests.py, templates, routes, system_detail_bridge.py, job.js/css were not modified."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":