's system_states() (only that function and its own new helpers _workup/_readiness_panel were touched) now requires, per system: own codes cleared (no ACTIVE) AND either no monitor (stays CLEARED_UNVERIFIED) or the relevant monitor(s) complete on a from-car dossier_bridge.readiness_panel reading (VERIFIED_CLEAN); the whole-car verdict is no longer consulted anywhere in this function.\n\nNew test cuore/tests/check_system_vocab.py covers: all 25 keys/labels + 16 aliases + junk/blank -> None; hypothesis add/edit normalization and old-record migration; mechanic_tests systems-vocabulary validity; and the three system_states scenarios (EVAP incomplete -> CLEARED_UNVERIFIED, EVAP complete from the car -> VERIFIED_CLEAN, demo-source readiness never -> VERIFIED_CLEAN), plus a no-monitor-system guard — using a synthetic by_system/dossier fixture (the real Stelvio corpus's EVAP codes are ACTIVE/returned, not CLEARED_UNVERIFIED, so it couldn't serve as the fixture for this specific check) with a deliberately VERIFIED_CLEAN whole-car verdict to prove no shortcut is taken.\n\nOne note for the template owner: job.html renders `h.system` directly (line 211/207) for display; that now shows the normalized lowercase key (e.g. \"evap\", or \"engine_management\" for a \"misfire\" family hypothesis) instead of the raw text a mechanic typed. The original text is preserved in the new `system_text` field for exactly this case — the template can switch to showing that instead when convenient. I did not touch job.html (templates are off-limits per my scope).\n\nFiles touched: mes-log-mcp/mes/systems.py, mes-log-mcp/mes/jobs.py, cuore/services/jobs_bridge.py, cuore/services/electrical_bridge.py, cuore/services/systems_map_bridge.py (system_states + its own helpers only), cuore/tests/check_system_vocab.py (new). mechanic_tests.py, templates, routes, system_detail_bridge.py, job.js/css were not modified."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"e58f3c6b-a8c2-4dd4-aace-8ea9f6678e18","apiBlockIndex":0,"reques